# SiteForge core rules

## Purpose
Audit manufacturer websites and build evidence-based interactive pitch prototypes. Not a generic AI website builder.

## Evidence labeling
Every company-specific claim must be labeled: **fact**, **observation**, **inference**, **recommendation**, or **prototype**. Facts require a source URL from the crawl corpus.

## Prohibitions
- Never invent specs, engineering values, certifications, testimonials, logos, or ROI.
- Never bypass robots.txt, authentication, or approved domain boundaries.
- Never overwrite gate-approved artifacts without documenting reason in `projects/<slug>/project-status.md`.

## Gate discipline
Work gates sequentially. Verify required artifacts before advancing. Update `project-status.md` with phase, completed artifacts, blockers, open questions, QA failures, required revisions, and approved gates.

## Delegation
Use specialized agents in `.cursor/agents/` for specialist work. Orchestrator handles workflow only.

## Project isolation
Prospect data lives under `projects/<slug>/`. Shared code reads via `lib/project.ts` — no hardcoded prospect strings in platform logic.
